ry AC maps to a module and a test; the data contracts match the real surfaces the design calls into (the LHC SDK at `packages/lhc`, the PI extension API at `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` v0.79.2, the completion API at `@earendil-works/pi-ai`). The tech-design questions are answered below, and the places where the design takes a position the epic left open are recorded as deviations with rationale.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:23:| I-2 | TDQ-2 | Fork derived-form reuse — provable-safe copy vs always-requeue. | **Resolved for v1: always requeue.** The new thread is seeded by event replay only; derived forms are not copied across the fork. Reuse is a later optimization gated on a provenance-identity check that does not exist yet. The epic's AC-3.3 permits this (reuse \"may\" happen; requeue is the correct fallback). Recorded as a deviation — the epic leaves the door open, the design closes it for v1. See Deferred Items. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:24:| I-3 | TDQ-3 | `thinkingSignature` / `thoughtSignature` handling. | **Resolved: capture, do not interpret.** Assistant thinking carries an opaque `thinkingSignature`; tool calls carry an opaque `thoughtSignature` (the POC mapper found both). Neither is part of the seven LHC intake payloads, which are text/structured-arg only. The converter records thinking text and tool-call arguments; the signatures are dropped in this epic because nothing in capture or derivation consumes them. Flagged as a deviation: re-injecting signatures is a serving concern (Epic 2), not capture. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:184:| `lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts` | NEW | Launch flags → registry resolution (new / `--session` full+partial / `--continue` most-recent); reload reconstructs from resolved id; unresolvable id fails loud | `lhc` threads | AC-1.2, AC-1.5, AC-1.6 |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution.md:149:#### Spec Deviations\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:1:// Story 2 — SV-001 regression: existing-thread resume/reload must keep recording\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:48:describe(\"Story 2: existing-thread reattach idempotency (SV-001)\", () => {\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/004-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"cdabf308-0529-4edb-9c42-8bdcdceb167e\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5d0-02af-7833-aa10-b5a891cf7379\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5d0-02af-7833-aa10-b5a891cf7379\",\"storyId\":\"03-capture-verification\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-capture-verification\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Capture Verification\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/03-capture-verification.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/003-implementor.json\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 3 against AC-6.1 through AC-6.3, the replay harness, corpus fixtures, verification tests, inspect/health evidence, and configured gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Replay does not compare actual message and turn read-back records\",\"evidence\":\"AC-6.1 requires the thread read-back — events, messages, and turns — to match fixture expectations. `replayCorpus` reads `intakeStream.listEvents` and `inspect.overview` only (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:282-291`). `compareReadback` compares event kind/payload order, then checks only `overview.messages.visible`, `overview.messages.byKind`, `overview.turns.closed`, and `overview.turns.open` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:219-260`). The SDK exposes actual message and turn read-back surfaces (`messages` and `turns` exports in `packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:1-4`, plus `MessageRecord`/`TurnRecord` types at `packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:173-182`), but the Story 3 harness and tests do not consume them. `test/verify/replay.test.ts` adds an extra TC-6.1 assertion for event kinds only (`packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts:86-91`). This leaves message content/order/turn association unverified despite the AC naming messages and turns explicitly.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Corpus replay uses synthetic flat messages and inferred lifecycle instead of recorded PI hook corpora\",\"evidence\":\"AC-6.1 is scoped to replaying recorded PI corpora. The fixture loader states that, until M0 delivers recordings, it builds synthetic stand-ins (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4`), and each named corpus source is an in-memory `AgentMessage[]` built with `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:21-29`, `42-53`, `69-83`, `97-105`, `118-124`). The replay harness source type is also just `AgentMessage[]` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:35-38`). During replay it synthesizes deterministic entry ids and infers `agent_end` boundaries from a new user prompt or end-of-stream (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:117-143`) instead of consuming recorded `message_end` / `agent_end` events with their original positions. That proves the converter on synthetic message shapes, but not replay fidelity for recorded PI corpora or recorded lifecycle ordering.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Replay does not compare actual message and turn read-back records\",\"evidence\":\"AC-6.1 requires the thread read-back — events, messages, and turns — to match fixture expectations. `replayCorpus` reads `intakeStream.listEvents` and `inspect.overview` only (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:282-291`). `compareReadback` compares event kind/payload order, then checks only `overview.messages.visible`, `overview.messages.byKind`, `overview.turns.closed`, and `overview.turns.open` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:219-260`). The SDK exposes actual message and turn read-back surfaces (`messages` and `turns` exports in `packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:1-4`, plus `MessageRecord`/`TurnRecord` types at `packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:173-182`), but the Story 3 harness and tests do not consume them. `test/verify/replay.test.ts` adds an extra TC-6.1 assertion for event kinds only (`packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts:86-91`). This leaves message content/order/turn association unverified despite the AC naming messages and turns explicitly.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Corpus replay uses synthetic flat messages and inferred lifecycle instead of recorded PI hook corpora\",\"evidence\":\"AC-6.1 is scoped to replaying recorded PI corpora. The fixture loader states that, until M0 delivers recordings, it builds synthetic stand-ins (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4`), and each named corpus source is an in-memory `AgentMessage[]` built with `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:21-29`, `42-53`, `69-83`, `97-105`, `118-124`). The replay harness source type is also just `AgentMessage[]` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:35-38`). During replay it synthesizes deterministic entry ids and infers `agent_end` boundaries from a new user prompt or end-of-stream (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:117-143`) instead of consuming recorded `message_end` / `agent_end` events with their original positions. That proves the converter on synthetic message shapes, but not replay fidelity for recorded PI corpora or recorded lifecycle ordering.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-6.2 / TC-6.2: deterministic replay and same-thread re-replay are covered by `test/verify/replay.test.ts`; full `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` passed with 79 tests.\",\"AC-6.3 / TC-6.3: inspect overview/health counts, last event span, capture gaps, and failed derivations are covered by `test/verify/replay.test.ts`; full `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` passed.\",\"Fixture validity risk for current fixture shapes: `test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts` validates well-formed expected event shapes and rejects a malformed corpus.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-6.1 / TC-6.1: actual `messages.listMessages` and `turns.listTurns` read-back records are not compared to fixture expectations.\",\"AC-6.1 / TC-6.1: recorded PI corpus lifecycle replay is not proven; current corpus sources are synthetic flat `AgentMessage[]` inputs with inferred boundaries.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\",\"result\":\"fail\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts` synthesizes entry ids and agent-run boundaries instead of replaying recorded hook lifecycle events, so the verification path is not yet proving recorded-corpus fidelity.\",\"`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts` does not use the real message and turn read-back surfaces, only overview counts for those sections.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[\"If M0 recorded corpora are still unavailable, does the impl lead want to explicitly accept synthetic stand-ins for this story, or should Story 3 remain blocked until those fixture inputs exist?\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Configured story gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` passed. `green-verify` failed only at `check-test-immutability.mjs` for four pre-existing Story 2 capture test files, matching the implementor's reported drift and not the configured Story 3 gate.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/004-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T11:06:44.123Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T11:11:24.963Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/05-inference-host-routing/003-implementor.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-implement\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"a47a279a-00cf-4d98-821c-1559c5c1f285\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"7894f3ec-841a-4c17-b9cf-403440004aac\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"7894f3ec-841a-4c17-b9cf-403440004aac\",\"storyId\":\"05-inference-host-routing\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"05-inference-host-routing\",\"title\":\"Story 5: Inference Host Routing\"},\"planSummary\":\"Implemented Story 5 (Inference Host Routing): createModelCall function that resolves (provider,model) via ctx.modelRegistry.find and completes through pi-ai's complete() API with failure classification. Implemented classifyFailure for terminal (auth, invalid_request) and retryable (rate_limit, timeout, network) failures plus thrown→other mapping. Created test/inference/model-call.test.ts with TC-4.1 through TC-4.4 covering routing, multi-lane, failure classification, and empty_output behavior. Created test/inference/closed-loop.test.ts with TC-4.5 proving capture→derivation→recorded-outcome loop with ready forms queryable via inspect/health. Added local pi-ai types (pi-ai.ts) as placeholder pending real dependency. Story gate passes (102 tests total, +19 tests for this story).\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\",\"reason\":\"Implemented createModelCall and classifyFailure functions per AC-4.1..4.4\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added local pi-ai type declarations pending real dependency (Spec Deviation)\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/model-call.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"TC-4.1..4.4 tests for routing, multi-lane, failure classification, empty_output\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/closed-loop.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"TC-4.5 closed-loop test proving capture→derivation→recorded-outcome\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"test/inference/model-call.test.ts\",\"test/inference/closed-loop.test.ts\"],\"modified\":[],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":102,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":19},\"gatesRun\