ssues raised by Reviewer 2. Per conservative reverify protocol, blockers are downgraded only when explicit evidence disproves them. The reverification examined the disputed surfaces: (1) Story 3's corpus verification path against AC-6.1's recorded PI corpora requirement; (2) Story 1's reload semantics against AC-1.5's exact-thread reconstruction requirement. Findings follow.\\\",\\n  \\\"crossStoryFindings\\\": [\\n    \\\"Stories 2-5 are coherent across the capture/fork/inference/startup-validation spine: all paths route through connector entry points and real LHC intake/scheduler/inspect surfaces (both reviewers agree).\\\",\\n    \\\"Story 1 has a lifecycle coverage gap: reload for no-flag and --resume launches reattaches by cwd-most-recent registry row, not by durable resolved-threadId reconstruction (Reviewer 2 block EV-002; Reviewer 1 NF-002 as accepted constraint).\\\",\\n    \\\"Story 3 does not satisfy the epic-level verification contract: corpus fixtures are simplified AgentMessage JSONL rows paired with handcrafted expected events, not recorded PI hook/lifecycle corpora as required by AC-6.1 (Reviewer 2 block EV-001; Reviewer 1 claims real corpora used).\\\",\\n    \\\"Plain-data-only rule is enforced across all lifecycle paths—SessionState contains only ThreadRef + flags, no PI objects retained (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Capture flow is consistent: index.ts orchestrates map → accumulate → batch flush through converter for all message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select hooks (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Fork detection and seeding logic properly wired in session_start handler with both hook-based and session-tree fallback evidence paths (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Startup validation correctly runs after instance creation but before capture begins, leaving capture running on validation failure per AC-5.3 (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"The --resume picker has an interactive ctx.ui.select path for multi-candidate scenarios, while headless multi-candidate resume remains fail-closed requiring explicit --session (Reviewer 2; not disputed).\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"architectureFindings\\\": [\\n    \\\"Module boundaries respected: check-boundaries.mjs passes (20 src files checked) (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Interfaces match tech design Interface Definitions—all required exports present with correct signatures (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Hook rail matches EPIC_1_HOOKS specification—all observe-only hooks registered, context hook correctly omitted (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Converter architecture matches tech design: map-message is pure, TurnAccumulator owns the LHC turn boundary, converter flushes through intakeStream.messageEvents (both reviewers agree).\\\",\\n    \\\"Local PI types in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified v0.79.2 contract since @earendil-works/* packages aren't build dependencies yet (Reviewer 1 NF-004; Reviewer 2 NF-002).\\\",\\n    \\\"initLhc is thin wrapper over createSdk per tech-arch A-4—mechanical rename pending LHC package change (Reviewer 1 NF-005).\\\",\\n    \\\"The observe-only boundary is preserved: index.ts registers no context hook, capture does not alter PI's model context path (Reviewer 2; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Derived-form reuse is deferred while fork correctness is preserved—fork requeues derived forms on new thread rather than copying/reusing per tech design I-2 (Reviewer 1 NF-003; Reviewer 2 NF-003).\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"epicCoverageAssessment\\\": [\\n    \\\"All 33 TCs mapped to tests—test-plan.md TC→Test mapping fully realized (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Architecture-risk tests present: 7 tests covering restart survival, idempotency double-replay, failure classification, capture isolation, fork source immutability, fixture validity, concurrency (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Foundation tests present: 7 tests covering corpus shapes, synthetic builders, temp-thread factory, extension-load smoke, verification-config (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Total test coverage: 144 tests passing across 20 test files (Reviewer 1; Reviewer 2 gates also passed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Flows 2-5 are covered by source and tests: ordered capture, turn derivation, idempotency, fork replay, model-call routing, classified failures, startup validation (Reviewer 2).\\\",\\n    \\\"Flow 1 is partially covered: launch creation, named resolution, continue, interactive resume, shutdown implemented; exact same-thread reload not implemented for no-flag and --resume launches (Reviewer 2).\\\",\\n    \\\"Flow 6 is incomplete against AC-6.1: replay is deterministic and compares events/messages/turns, but does not consume recorded PI corpora as required (Reviewer 2 EV-001).\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"productionPathFindings\\\": [\\n    \\\"Production createModelCall uses real PI modelRegistry.find and hasConfiguredAuth—no fake adapters in production inference path (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Extension entry point (index.ts activate) registers real hooks with production defaults (~/.lhc registry, process.argv launch flags, real ModelCall) (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"No shims or placeholders in production capture path—converter, idempotency, turn-accumulator all use real implementations (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Startup validation uses real PI modelRegistry for reachability probes—correctly classifies unknown_model vs auth_not_configured (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Test-only model-call fakes are confined to packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures and are not production code (Reviewer 2; not disputed).\\\",\\n    \\\"Material non-real verification path: packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl are simplified AgentMessage rows with no PI hook metadata or lifecycle events, and packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts hand-builds expected events instead of replaying recorded PI hook/lifecycle corpora (