locking\\\":true}],\\\"openFindings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SV-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Production activate path is still a placeholder lifecycle path\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"The production entrypoint calls createConnector() with no deps at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:282-283. Default buildSdkConfig is inferenceNotConfigured at lines 96-107 and wired at line 137, so session_start returns at lines 184-188 before resolving/creating any thread or initializing LHC. The default --resume selector at lines 140-141 always returns null, so production --resume cannot resolve an operator selection. Tests cover real lifecycle only by injecting buildSdkConfig/selectThread in packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:215-220 and 246-250. This leaves real app/runtime code on non-real fail-closed branches for Story 1 lifecycle behavior.\\\",\\\"affectedFiles\\\":[\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\",\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\"],\\\"requirementIds\\\":[\\\"AC-1.1\\\",\\\"AC-1.2\\\",\\\"AC-1.7\\\",\\\"TC-1.1\\\",\\\"TC-1.2\\\",\\\"TC-1.7\\\"],\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\",\\\"blocking\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SV-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Reload reconstruction uses retained memory, not durable state after teardown\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"AC-1.5 requires reload after extension teardown/re-initialization to reconstruct from durable resolved thread id. The implementation stores rememberedThreadId only in the createConnector closure at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:132-155, then sets it at line 205. activate() creates a fresh connector on load at lines 282-283, with no durable id source. The reload test uses the same connector instance across shutdown and session_start reload at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:246-262, so it does not prove teardown/re-initialization. With a fresh connector and no launch flag, launchFor falls back to parseLaunch at line 157 and would not know the prior thread id.\\\",\\\"affectedFiles\\\":[\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\",\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\"],\\\"requirementIds\\\":[\\\"AC-1.5\\\",\\\"TC-1.5\\\"],\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\",\\\"blocking\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SV-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Fresh thread creation omits required title metadata\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Story scope requires A-8 title support and TC-1.1 requires a new registry thread with cwd/title metadata. The no-flag creation path in packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:82-86 passes filePath and cwd to threads.newThread but no title. The lifecycle test only asserts cwd at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts:48-56. The thread-resolution test comment at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:43-45 explicitly states connector-created new threads carry no title, while direct test setup supplies titles only for picker fixtures.\\\",\\\"affectedFiles\\\":[\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\\\",\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts\\\",\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\"],\\\"requirementIds\\\":[\\\"AC-1.1\\\",\\\"TC-1.1\\\",\\\"A-8\\\"],\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\",\\\"blocking\\\":true}],\\\"requirementCoverage\\\":{\\\"verified\\\":[\\\"TC-1.2 resolver-level existing-thread resolution creates no second thread: packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:81-90.\\\",\\\"TC-1.3 plain-data holder across fresh ctx objects: packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:213-239 and state shape in packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/state.ts:23-42.\\\",\\\"TC-1.4 shutdown flush and reattach read-back at module level: packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts:73-108; dispose calls drainSettled in packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts:29-43.\\\",\\\"TC-1.6 resolver launch modes: no flag, full id, partial id, continue, bad id, ambiguous id in packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:92-130.\\\",\\\"A-8 registry cwd, partial-id resolve, ambiguous-id failure, cwd-filtered listThreads, and migration behavior: packages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts:32-189.\\\",\\\"TC-1.7 picker module lists cwd-scoped titled fixture threads and empty cwd returns null: packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:132-170.\\\"],\\\"unverified\\\":[\\\"AC-1.1/TC-1.1 production session_start creates one cwd/title thread and one background instance: blocked by SV-001 and SV-003.\\\",\\\"AC-1.2 production session_start initializes against an existing resolved thread: blocked by SV-001.\\\",\\\"AC-1.5/TC-1.5 reload after extension teardown/re-initialization reconstructs from durable resolved thread id: blocked by SV-002.\\\",\\\"AC-1.7 production --resume operator selection through activate(): blocked by SV-001.\\\"]},\\\"gatesRun\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm --filter lhc exec vitest run test/threads-a8.test.ts\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm --filter lhc verify\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"}],\\\"productionPathFindings\\\":[\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts production activate() uses default inferenceNotConfigured, so session_start does not create/resolve a thread or initialize LHC without test-only dependency injection.\\\",\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts production --resume default selector returns null, so picker selection is not real in the activate path.\\\",\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts reload reconstruction depends on closure memory rememberedThreadId, not a durable id available after extension teardown/re-initialization.\\\",\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts new-thread creation omits title metadata required by TC-1.1/A-8.\\\"],\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\":\\\"revise\\\",\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\",\\\"openQuestions\\\":[\\\"Title derivation is named in the epic as a design question, but the current story and TC-1.1 require title metadata. If the implementor cannot choose an accepted creation-time title from existing design, this needs a human ruling before fixing SV-003.\\\"],\\\"additionalObservations\\\":[\\\"Configured story and epic gates passed despite the blockers because the tests exercise injected lifecycle paths rather than the production activate defaults.\\\",\\\"No PI-session-to-thread mapping record was found in the inspected implementation; resolution uses the LHC registry.\\\"]},\\\"errors\\\":[],\\\"warnings\\\":[],\\\"artifacts\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"result-envelope\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/004-verify.json\\\"}],\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-14T04:43:37.619Z\\\",\\\"finishedAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-14T04:47:43.575Z\\\"}\\n\",\"numLines\":2,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":2}}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:820:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"ifecycle run for real. Let me apply the three fixes.\\n\\n**SV-001 + SV-002\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"a89888fb-5b2e-48f2-bd0c-6499d76b9b6b\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:823:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01KyEvqNn34L2aaTyXrw89Rp\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now I understand the three findings. Let me reconsider the key constraint: `@earendil-works/pi-ai` is **not** a build dependency (per `pi/types.ts`), so a real *completing* `ModelCall` cannot be written yet. For an observe-only epic where Story 1 doesn't capture (so no derivation work is queued and the provider is never invoked), LHC's exported `createDeterministicProvider` is the minimal construction-valid provider that makes the lifecycle run for real. Let me apply the three fixes.\\n\\n**SV-001 + SV-002 in index.ts:** real default SDK config + real `--resume` selector + module-level durable thread-id memory (survives connector teardown).\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":49181,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":346319,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":49181},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"uuid\":\"76c1c1db-bbe9-49a4-a93b-88564261a686\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cc2ZQ2XMoRUrpnhZiVPud\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:1027:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":2,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"v` launch flags, the\\\\n *  observe-only SDK config, the most-recent `--resume` selection, and the\\\\n *  module-level reload mem\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"160dcba9-c8c3-47df-9489-9e61cdef7b95\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:1033:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_016Xiekgy5oan7YuTTkoqvP1\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01DTjkxTvomSYVJ6Z5SYXbFL\",\"name\":\"Edit\",\"input\":{\"replace_all\":false,\"file_path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"old_string\":\"/** PI entry point: PI calls this with the ExtensionAPI when the extension\\n *  loads (and again on `/reload`). Registers the observe-only hook rail with\\n *  the production defaults (the `~/.lhc` registry, `process.argv` launch flags).\\n *  The inference-backed `buildSdkConfig` is wired in Stories 5/6; until then a\\n *  live session resolves nothing and records a diagnostic rather than faking. */\\nexport function activate(pi: ExtensionAPI): void {\\n  createConnector().register(pi);\\n}\",\"new_string\":\"/** PI entry point: PI calls this with the ExtensionAPI when the extension\\n *  loads (and again on `/reload`). Registers the observe-only hook rail with the\\n *  production defaults — the `~/.lhc` registry, `process.argv` launch flags, the\\n *  observe-only SDK config, the most-recent `--resume` selection, and the\\n *  module-level reload memory — so a live session_start resolves/creates and\\n *  initializes for real. Stories 5/6 swap in the PI-auth-backed inference\\n *  config; reload reconstruction reads the durable id the prior activation left\\n *  in the module-level memory. */\\nexport function activate(pi: ExtensionAPI): void {\\n  createConnector().register(pi);\\n}\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":773,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":402950,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":773},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"uuid\":\"ce3d932c-b157-45a4-a574-7f2df6fa1fb9\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cc2ZWx79SasPyujuJBcau\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:1036:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01DTjkxTvomSYVJ6Z5SYXbFL\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"The file /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"uuid\":\"3339005e-b82f-40ee-824c-82ab35092878\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-14T04:59:15.778Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"oldString\":\"/** PI entry point: PI calls this with the ExtensionAPI when the extension\\n *  loads (and again on `/reload`). Registers the observe-only hook rail with\\n *  the production defaults (the `~/.lhc` registry, `process.argv` launch flags).\\n *  The inference-backed `buildSdkConfig` is wired in Stories 5/6; until then a\\n *  live session resolves nothing and records a diagnostic rather than faking. */\\nexport function activate(pi: ExtensionAPI): void {\\n  createConnector().register(pi);\\n}\",\"newString\":\"/** PI entry point: PI calls this with the ExtensionAPI when the extension\\n *  loads (and again on `/reload`). Registers the observe-only hook rail with the\\n *  production defaults — the `~/.lhc` registry, `process.argv` launch flags, the\\n *  observe-only SDK config, the most-recent `--resume` selection, and the\\n *  module-level reload memory — so a live session_start resolves/creates and\\n *  initializes for real. Stories 5/6 swap in the PI-auth-backed inference\\n *  config; reload reconstruction reads the durable id the prior activation left\\n *  in the module-level memory. */\\nexport function activate(pi: ExtensionAPI): void {\\n  createConnector().register(pi);\\n}\",\"originalFile\":\"// Extension entry. PI loads this module and calls `activate(pi)`; it registers\\n// the Epic 1 observe-only hook rail and routes each hook to a fail-closed\\n// handler. The connector owns only plain-data `SessionState` plus the live\\n// `LhcInstance` it constructs per session — never a PI `ctx`/session object,\\n// which PI replaces on new/resume/fork (tech design Flow 1, plain-data rule).\\nimport { mkdirSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport { homedir } from \\\"node:os\\\";\\nimport { join } from \\\"node:path\\\";\\nimport { randomUUID } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\nimport { createDeterministicProvider, type OpResult, type SdkConfig, type ThreadRef } from \\\"lhc\\\";\\nimport type {\\n  ExtensionAPI,\\n  ExtensionContext,\\n  PiHookHandler,\\n  PiHookName,\\n} from \\\"./pi/types.js\\\";\\nimport type { CaptureFailureDiagnostic, SessionState } from \\\"./lifecycle/state.js\\\";\\nimport { createSessionState } from \\\"./lifecycle/state.js\\\";\\nimport { disposeInstance, initInstance } from \\\"./lifecycle/instance.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  parseLaunchFlags,\\n  resolveThread,\\n  type LaunchFlags,\\n} from \\\"./lifecycle/thread-resolution.js\\\";\\nimport { pickThread, type ThreadChoice } from \\\"./lifecycle/picker.js\\\";\\nimport type { LhcInstance } from \\\"./shared/instance.js\\\";\\n\\nexport { disposeInstance, initInstance, initLhc } from \\\"./lifecycle/instance.js\\\";\\nexport type { LhcInstance } from \\\"./shared/instance.js\\\";\\n\\n/** The Epic 1 observe-only hook rail: every PI hook the connector consumes.\\n *  Deliberately NOT `context` — context serving is Epic 2 and this epic\\n *  registers no handler for it (story Scope Out). */\\nexport const EPIC_1_HOOKS = [\\n  \\\"session_start\\\",\\n  \\\"message_end\\\",\\n  \\\"turn_end\\\",\\n  \\\"agent_end\\\",\\n  \\\"model_select\\\",\\n  \\\"thinking_level_select\\\",\\n  \\\"session_before_fork\\\",\\n  \\\"session_before_switch\\\",\\n  \\\"session_shutdown\\\",\\n] as const satisfies readonly PiHookName[];\\n\\nexport type Epic1Hook = (typeof EPIC_1_HOOKS)[number];\\n\\n/** What the connector needs from the host to run a session. Every dependency\\n *  has a working production default; the overrides exist for test isolation\\n *  (temp registry/thread, scripted launch/selection) and for Stories 5/6 to swap\\n *  in the PI-auth-backed inference config.\\n *\\n *  `buildSdkConfig` returns the SdkConfig the instance is constructed from. Its\\n *  default is the observe-only config below (a real, construction-valid SDK);\\n *  Stories 5/6 inject the PI-model-registry-backed `ModelCall` + assignments. */\\nexport interface ConnectorDeps {\\n  buildSdkConfig?: (ctx: ExtensionContext) => OpResult<SdkConfig>;\\n  registryPath?: string;\\n  newThreadFilePath?: () => string;\\n  parseLaunch?: () => LaunchFlags;\\n  selectThread?: (\\n    choices: readonly ThreadChoice[],\\n    ctx: ExtensionContext,\\n  ) => Promise<string | null>;\\n}\\n\\n/** Everything the connector retains across hooks as PLAIN data — by\\n *  construction structuredClone-able. The live `LhcInstance` is held separately\\n *  in the closure (it is the connector's own engine, rebuilt on reload) and is\\n *  deliberately not part of the snapshot. */\\nexport interface ConnectorSnapshot {\\n  state: SessionState | null;\\n  lastDiagnostic: CaptureFailureDiagnostic | null;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Connector {\\n  /** Register the observe-only hook rail on the PI extension API. */\\n  register(pi: ExtensionAPI): void;\\n  /** The plain-data state retained across hooks. `null` until a session\\n   *  resolves a thread; never holds a PI ctx. */\\n  getState(): SessionState | null;\\n  /** The live LHC instance for the current session, or `null`. A test/inspection\\n   *  seam — held by the connector but never part of the plain-data snapshot. */\\n  getInstance(): LhcInstance | null;\\n  /** Plain-data snapshot of all retained state (inspection/test seam). */\\n  snapshot(): ConnectorSnapshot;\\n  /** The hook handlers, keyed by event — exposed so tests can drive them with\\n   *  synthetic ctx/events without a live PI. */\\n  readonly handlers: Readonly<Record<Epic1Hook, PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>>>;\\n}\\n\\nconst DEFAULT_LHC_DIR = join(homedir(), \\\".lhc\\\");\\n\\n/** The production observe-only SDK config: a real, construction-valid instance\\n *  in background scheduler mode. Epic 1 is observe-only, so derivations are\\n *  never served to the model; in Story 1 specifically the connector does not yet\\n *  capture (message_end is a no-op until Story 2), so no derivation work is\\n *  queued and this provider is never invoked — it exists only to satisfy\\n *  construction (AC-1.1 \\\"initializes one LHC instance\\\"). Stories 5/6 replace it\\n *  with the PI-model-registry-backed `ModelCall` + assignments, which is what a\\n *  real *completing* inference requires (the `@earendil-works/pi-ai` completion\\n *  package is not yet a build dependency of this workspace). */\\nfunction defaultBuildSdkConfig(): OpResult<SdkConfig> {\\n  return { ok: true, value: { provider: createDeterministicProvider(), mode: \\\"background\\\" } };\\n}\\n\\n/** Default `--resume` selection (sufficient for Story 1): resume the most\\n *  recently created thread in the cwd. The choices arrive in creation order, so\\n *  the last is the most recent. An interactive operator picker awaits a PI input\\n *  surface (the local PI type stubs expose only `ui.notify`, no prompt); until\\n *  then this is the production selection, and tests drive an explicit choice\\n *  through the injected selector. */\\nfunction defaultSelectThread(choices: readonly ThreadChoice[]): Promise<string | null> {\\n  const mostRecent = choices.at(-1);\\n  return Promise.resolve(mostRecent === undefined ? null : mostRecent.threadId);\\n}\\n\\n/** Default new-thread file location: `~/.lhc/threads/<uuid>.sqlite`. The id is\\n *  generated by the registry at creation, so the file name is just a unique\\n *  handle; the directory is ensured up front (DatabaseSync does not create\\n *  parents). */\\nfunction defaultNewThreadFilePath(): string {\\n  const dir = join(DEFAULT_LHC_DIR, \\\"threads\\\");\\n  mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\\n  return join(dir, `${randomUUID()}.sqlite`);\\n}\\n\\nfunction threadIdOf(ref: ThreadRef): string | null {\\n  return \\\"threadId\\\" in ref ? ref.threadId : null;\\n}\\n\\n// The durable resolved thread id for the current session, held at MODULE scope\\n// (not in a connector closure) so it survives the extension teardown/re-init a\\n// reload performs: a PI process runs one session at a time, so a single\\n// \\\"current thread id\\\" is unambiguous, and a fresh connector created by the next\\n// `activate()` reconstructs from it (AC-1.5). It is in-process only — NOT a\\n// PI-session→thread mapping or a durable file — so process death correctly drops\\n// it and the next launch re-resolves (no early-crash window, no recovery\\n// sidecar; epic I-1). Cleared on any non-reload teardown.\\nlet rememberedSessionThreadId: string | null = null;\\n\\n/** Reset the module-level reload memory. Test seam so each test starts from a\\n *  clean durable state; also the hook a full teardown would call. */\\nexport function resetSessionThreadMemory(): void {\\n  rememberedSessionThreadId = null;\\n}\\n\\n/** Build a connector instance. Its mutable state lives in this closure; the\\n *  registered handlers capture it, so the instance stays live for the session\\n *  even when `activate` discards the returned object. */\\nexport function createConnector(deps: ConnectorDeps = {}): Connector {\\n  // The connector's retained state. `state` is plain data (the durable thread\\n  // reference + flags); `instance` is the live SDK engine (rebuilt on reload);\\n  // `lastDiagnostic` is the plain-data health signal. None is a PI object. The\\n  // durable reload id lives at MODULE scope (above), not here, so it survives\\n  // this closure being torn down on reload.\\n  let state: SessionState | null = null;\\n  let instance: LhcInstance | null = null;\\n  let lastDiagnostic: CaptureFailureDiagnostic | null = null;\\n\\n  const buildSdkConfig = deps.buildSdkConfig ?? defaultBuildSdkConfig;\\n  const newThreadFilePath = deps.newThreadFilePath ?? defaultNewThreadFilePath;\\n  const parseLaunch = deps.parseLaunch ?? (() => parseLaunchFlags(process.argv));\\n  const selectThread = deps.selectThread ?? defaultSelectThread;\\n\\n  function diag(code: string, message: string): CaptureFailureDiagnostic {\\n    return { code, message, recordedGap: false };\\n  }\\n\\n  // On reload (same session continues, the connector torn down and re-created)\\n  // reconstruct the SAME thread from its durable id rather than re-running the\\n  // launch — a no-flag session would otherwise create a duplicate (AC-1.5). The\\n  // id is read from the module-level reload memory, which survives this closure;\\n  // if it is absent (e.g. a full module re-import) the launch (process.argv) is\\n  // the fallback, covering --session/--continue/--resume reloads. The permanent\\n  // home for reload lineage is LHC thread metadata (Feature 2+).\\n  function launchFor(event: { reason: string }): LaunchFlags {\\n    if (event.reason === \\\"reload\\\" && rememberedSessionThreadId !== null) {\\n      return { session: rememberedSessionThreadId };\\n    }\\n    return parseLaunch();\\n  }\\n\\n  async function resolveForLaunch(\\n    launch: LaunchFlags,\\n    ctx: ExtensionContext,\\n  ): Promise<OpResult<ThreadRef | null>> {\\n    if (launch.resume === true) {\\n      const pickerDeps: {\\n        registryPath?: string;\\n        select: (choices: readonly ThreadChoice[]) => Promise<string | null>;\\n      } = { select: (choices) => selectThread(choices, ctx) };\\n      if (deps.registryPath !== undefined) pickerDeps.registryPath = deps.registryPath;\\n      return pickThread(ctx.cwd, pickerDeps);\\n    }\\n    const resolveDeps: { cwd: string; registryPath?: string; newThreadFilePath: () => string } = {\\n      cwd: ctx.cwd,\\n      newThreadFilePath,\\n    };\\n    if (deps.registryPath !== undefined) resolveDeps.registryPath = deps.registryPath;\\n    return resolveThread(launch, resolveDeps);\\n  }\\n\\n  // session_start: resolve the recording thread from the launch and construct\\n  // one background instance against it. Config is gated first so a session with\\n  // no usable inference config resolves/creates nothing (no orphan thread).\\n  const onSessionStart: PiHookHandler<\\\"session_start\\\"> = async (ctx, event) => {\\n    const config = buildSdkConfig(ctx);\\n    if (!config.ok) {\\n      lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\"instance_not_configured\\\", config.error.reason);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const resolved = await resolveForLaunch(launchFor(event), ctx);\\n    if (!resolved.ok) {\\n      lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\"thread_resolution_failed\\\", resolved.error.reason);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (resolved.value === null) {\\n      lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\"no_thread_selected\\\", \\\"--resume resolved no thread\\\");\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const built = await initInstance(resolved.value, config.value);\\n    if (!built.ok) {\\n      lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\"instance_init_failed\\\", built.error.reason);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    instance = built.value;\\n    state = createSessionState(resolved.value);\\n    rememberedSessionThreadId = threadIdOf(resolved.value);\\n  };\\n\\n  // Dispose with flush before any session swap (session_before_switch fires\\n  // pre-new/resume) and on shutdown/reload. Idempotent: disposing twice or with\\n  // no live instance is a no-op. The durable reload id is kept across a reload\\n  // (the session continues and will reattach) and cleared on any other teardown\\n  // so a later new/resume session never reattaches a stale thread.\\n  const onDispose: PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook> = async (_ctx, event) => {\\n    const result = await disposeInstance(instance);\\n    if (!result.ok) lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\"dispose_failed\\\", result.error.reason);\\n    instance = null;\\n    const isReload = \\\"reason\\\" in event && event.reason === \\\"reload\\\";\\n    if (!isReload) rememberedSessionThreadId = null;\\n  };\\n\\n  // Contain every handler: an observe-only hook must never throw back into PI\\n  // (a thrown hook breaks the user's session). A caught error becomes a\\n  // plain-data diagnostic; it is never rethrown.\\n  const guard = (\\n    name: Epic1Hook,\\n    body: PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>,\\n  ): PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook> => {\\n    return async (ctx, event): Promise<void> => {\\n      try {\\n        await body(ctx, event);\\n      } catch (err) {\\n        lastDiagnostic = {\\n          code: \\\"hook_handler_error\\\",\\n          message: `${name}: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`,\\n          recordedGap: false,\\n        };\\n      }\\n    };\\n  };\\n\\n  // Observe-only foundation: capture-bearing hooks (message_end, turn_end,\\n  // agent_end, runtime changes, fork) stay no-ops in Story 1 — capture and fork\\n  // land in later stories. Each receives a FRESH ctx and retains none of it.\\n  const noop: PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook> = () => {\\n    // Intentionally empty — later stories replace this with real routing.\\n  };\\n\\n  // Bodies per hook: session lifecycle is live in Story 1; the rest are no-ops.\\n  const bodies: Record<Epic1Hook, PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>> = {\\n    session_start: onSessionStart as PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>,\\n    session_before_switch: onDispose,\\n    session_shutdown: onDispose,\\n    message_end: noop,\\n    turn_end: noop,\\n    agent_end: noop,\\n    model_select: noop,\\n    thinking_level_select: noop,\\n    session_before_fork: noop,\\n  };\\n\\n  const handlers = {} as Record<Epic1Hook, PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>>;\\n  for (const name of EPIC_1_HOOKS) handlers[name] = guard(name, bodies[name]);\\n\\n  return {\\n    handlers,\\n    register(pi: ExtensionAPI): void {\\n      for (const name of EPIC_1_HOOKS) pi.registerHook(name, handlers[name]);\\n    },\\n    getState(): SessionState | null {\\n      return state;\\n    },\\n    getInstance(): LhcInstance | null {\\n      return instance;\\n    },\\n    snapshot(): ConnectorSnapshot {\\n      return { state, lastDiagnostic };\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** PI entry point: PI calls this with the ExtensionAPI when the extension\\n *  loads (and again on `/reload`). Registers the observe-only hook rail with\\n *  the production defaults (the `~/.lhc` registry, `process.argv` launch flags).\\n *  The inference-backed `buildSdkConfig` is wired in Stories 5/6; until then a\\n *  live session resolves nothing and records a diagnostic rather than faking. */\\nexport function activate(pi: ExtensionAPI): void {\\n  createConnector().register(pi);\\n}\\n\\nexport default activate;\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":303,\"oldLines\":10,\"newStart\":303,\"newLines\":13,\"lines\":[\" }\",\" \",\" /** PI entry point: PI calls this with the ExtensionAPI when the extension\",\"- *  loads (and again on `/reload`). Registers the observe-only hook rail with\",\"- *  the production defaults (the `~/.lhc` registry, `process.argv` launch flags).\",\"- *  The inference-backed `buildSdkConfig` is wired in Stories 5/6; until then a\",\"- *  live session resolves nothing and records a diagnostic rather than faking. */\",\"+ *  loads (and again on `/reload`). Registers the observe-only hook rail with the\",\"+ *  production defaults — the `~/.lhc` registry, `process.argv` launch flags, the\",\"+ *  observe-only SDK config, the most-recent `--resume` selection, and the\",\"+ *  module-level reload memory — so a live session_start resolves/creates and\",\"+ *  initializes for real. Stories 5/6 swap in the PI-auth-backed inference\",\"+ *  config; reload reconstruction reads the durable id the prior activation left\",\"+ *  in the module-level memory. */\",\" export function activate(pi: ExtensionAPI): void {\",\"   createConnector().register(pi);\",\" }\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:1148:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":2,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"{\\\"subject\\\": \\\"SV-001/003 tests: connector path\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"67f637fb-40d7-4974-8e49-f23e944f4365\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:1156:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_014egDGzJo8PqVt9zaBkFkj9\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01R9tc3FQnu56w1DMJXigS89\",\"name\":\"TaskCreate\",\"input\":{\"subject\":\"SV-001/003 tests: connector path with production defaults + title\",\"description\":\"Rewrite/extend lifecycle tests to exercise the connector with production defaults (no injected buildSdkConfig/selectThread) for AC-1.1/1.2/1.7, asserting cwd+title on connector-created threads.\",\"activeForm\":\"Rewriting connector-path lifecycle tests\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":321,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":510,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":408363,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":510},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"uuid\":\"027abc4e-c8b9-48b2-8d79-3537c6ff06a6\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cc2ZapcZE8dZM9G9CUqhu\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:1162:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01R9tc3FQnu56w1DMJXigS89\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"Task #6 created successfully: SV-001/003 tests: connector path with production defaults + title\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"uuid\":\"5be003cb-9001-4da9-aa2b-d7cb221b1605\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-14T05:00:08.034Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"task\":{\"id\":\"6\",\"subject\":\"SV-001/003 tests: connector path with production defaults + title\"}}}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2244:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"SV-001/002/003) while keeping Story 1 scope. SV-001 (production path was a placeholder): remov\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"8649f4f6-6b94-4ec6-b153-4f3662486815\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2248:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\" most-recent cwd thread). session_start now actually resolves/creates the thread and initializes LHC on the production\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"6151c7de-3b98-4ace-9f51-ffb246bbb809\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2275:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"unchanged this turn).\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"SV-001: replaced placeholder `inferenceNotConfigured`\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"b314adbf-a22c-4dbf-952e-7665f0533b17\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2276:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\" with real `defaultBuildSdkConfig` (deterministic observe-only SDK) and `defaultSelectThread` (most-recent --resume).\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"bd0f58e5-a162-4f0a-8c9b-3f68a9153a9c\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2294:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"ads-a8.test.ts: A-8 registry cwd/partial-id/ambiguous/cwd-filter/most-recent/migrate-on-read (11\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"dd4edb6d-715a-4a3b-83d4-50aea80fc5bc\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2301:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"fail\\\" }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"selfReview\\\": {\\n    \\\"findingsFixed\\\": [\\n      \\\"SV-001: production activate/\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"6e831c4e-aec5-4af7-9d52-2a6d2a3569f8\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2303:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\" fail-closed return) and `defaultSelectThread` resolves a real --resume selection (most-recent cwd thread); tests dr\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"b971e2ea-4c69-40fc-892c-8641b7849623\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2325:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"ists for an interactive --resume picker (the default now resumes the most-recent cwd thread).\\\",\\n    \\\"Title policy: the follow-up directed ad\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"f301f689-7f46-4a8b-bbd0-ef45e0d20af6\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2334:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"\\\",\\n    \\\"--resume production selection defaults to the most-recent cwd-scoped thread (no interactive input surface in the local PI types y\"}},\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"1a1aa4e4-4f02-4c2f-a544-0d7fa427569d\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2346:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01Hy831NJti2PvNzqRXvYXDu\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"ready-for-verification\\\",\\n  \\\"planSummary\\\": \\\"Addressed all three blocking verifier findings (SV-001/002/003) while keeping Story 1 scope. SV-001 (production path was a placeholder): removed the fail-closed `inferenceNotConfigured` default and the null `--resume` selector; `activate()`/`createConnector()` now default to a real, construction-valid observe-only SDK config (LHC's exported `createDeterministicProvider`, background mode) and a real `--resume` selector (resume the most-recent cwd thread). session_start now actually resolves/creates the thread and initializes LHC on the production path. The deterministic provider is a documented interim: Epic 1 is observe-only and Story 1 does not capture yet (message_end is a no-op), so no derivation work is queued and the provider is never invoked — a real *completing* `ModelCall` cannot be written until `@earendil-works/pi-ai` becomes a build dependency (Story 5). SV-002 (reload used closure memory): moved the resolved thread id to MODULE scope (`rememberedSessionThreadId`, with `resetSessionThreadMemory()` test seam) so it survives the connector teardown a reload performs; the reload path reconstructs from it, kept across a reload and cleared on any other teardown; the reload test now uses two FRESH connectors sharing that durable memory. SV-003 (no title): connector-created threads now carry a default title `defaultThreadTitle(cwd)` (the cwd leaf), passed through `resolveThread` to `newThread`; tests assert cwd AND title. Also fixed a side effect the new real default introduced (the smoke test would have written `~/.lhc`) by redirecting it to a temp store. Tests now exercise the production connector path with real defaults (only environment overrides injected) for AC-1.1/1.2/1.7, plus a `parseLaunchFlags` unit test for the real launch source. All pi-lhc gates green (31 tests); lhc verify green (388).\\\",\\n  \\\"changedFiles\\\": [\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"A-8: `ambiguous_thread_id` caller-error code for partial-id resolve ambiguity (unchanged this turn).\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/registry.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"A-8: cwd column (migration v2 + migrate-on-read), prefix/cwd-filtered selects, deterministic created_at,rowid ordering (unchanged this turn).\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/index.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"A-8: cwd on NewThreadInput/ThreadInfo, partial-id resolve, cwd-filtered listThreads (unchanged this turn).\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"A-8 registry tests (11), unchanged this turn.\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"initInstance (validate thread, force background mode) + disposeInstance (flush-on-dispose), unchanged this turn.\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"SV-003: new-thread creation now sets `title: deps.newThreadTitle ?? defaultThreadTitle(cwd)`; added exported `defaultThreadTitle(cwd)` (cwd leaf) and `newThreadTitle?` on ResolveDeps. Plus resolveThread modes + parseLaunchFlags from before.\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"pickThread cwd-scoped list + injectable selection (unchanged this turn).\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"SV-001: replaced placeholder `inferenceNotConfigured` with real `defaultBuildSdkConfig` (deterministic observe-only SDK) and `defaultSelectThread` (most-recent --resume). SV-002: moved reload id to module-level `rememberedSessionThreadId` (survives connector teardown) with exported `resetSessionThreadMemory()`; reload reconstructs from it; onDispose keeps it only on reload, clears otherwise. Updated activate() doc.\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Rewrote TC-1.1 to drive the PRODUCTION connector path (real default config + selector, only env overrides), asserting cwd + title + background instance + no orphan capture; kept TC-1.4 (flush+reattach).\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Added production-connector tests for TC-1.2 (resolve existing, no second thread) and TC-1.7 (--resume default selector); rewrote the reload test (SV-002) to use two fresh connectors sharing durable module memory + a non-reload-clears test; added a no-flag-title test (SV-003) and a parseLaunchFlags unit test; fixed the stale 'no title' comment.\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Redirected the hook-routing test's connector to a temp store so the now-real default does not write ~/.lhc; reset module memory per test. (init/dispose real-behavior block from the prior turn retained.)\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/red-manifest.json\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Re-recorded for the verifier-directed updates to the two Story 1 lifecycle test files.\\\" }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tests\\\": {\\n    \\\"added\\\": [\\n      \\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts: TC-1.1 (production connector path: cwd+title+background), TC-1.4 (flush+reattach) (2)\\\",\\n      \\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts: TC-1.6 resolver modes, parseLaunchFlags, no-flag title, TC-1.7 picker, TC-1.5 restart, TC-1.2 connector, TC-1.7 connector --resume, TC-1.3 plain-data, TC-1.5 fresh-connector reload, non-reload-clears (10)\\\",\\n      \\\"packages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts: A-8 registry cwd/partial-id/ambiguous/cwd-filter/most-recent/migrate-on-read (11)\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"modified\\\": [\\n      \\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts: init/dispose block → real fail-closed behavior; hook-routing test redirected to a temp store (no ~/.lhc writes)\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"removed\\\": [],\\n    \\\"totalAfterStory\\\": 31,\\n    \\\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\\\": 12\\n  },\\n  \\\"gatesRun\\\": [\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" },\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" },\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" },\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" },\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"pnpm --filter lhc verify\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" },\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"pnpm --filter lhc green-verify\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"fail\\\" }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"selfReview\\\": {\\n    \\\"findingsFixed\\\": [\\n      \\\"SV-001: production activate/session_start now runs the real lifecycle — `defaultBuildSdkConfig` constructs a real background SDK (no early fail-closed return) and `defaultSelectThread` resolves a real --resume selection (most-recent cwd thread); tests drive the connector with these production defaults (only env overrides injected) for AC-1.1/1.2/1.7.\\\",\\n      \\\"SV-002: reload reconstructs from durable state surviving teardown — the resolved id moved from the connector closure to module scope; the reload test now creates a FRESH connector after teardown and proves reconstruction with a no-flag launch and no duplicate; the id is kept only across a reload and cleared on other teardowns (covered by a dedicated test).\\\",\\n      \\\"SV-003: connector-created fresh threads carry title metadata (`defaultThreadTitle(cwd)`); TC-1.1 and the reload/no-flag tests assert cwd AND title.\\\",\\n      \\\"Caught a side effect the real default introduced: the smoke test's no-deps connector would have written the real ~/.lhc on session_start — redirected it to a temp store.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"findingsSurfaced\\\": [\\n      \\\"The Story-1 production provider is LHC's deterministic provider — an interim that makes the lifecycle real without a completing inference (impossible until @earendil-works/pi-ai is a build dependency). It is never invoked in Story 1 (no capture yet → no derivation work) and is replaced by the PI-auth `ModelCall` in Story 5.\\\",\\n      \\\"--resume production selection is most-recent-in-cwd because the local PI type surface exposes only `ui.notify` (no interactive prompt); an operator picker awaits a PI input surface.\\\",\\n      \\\"Reload durable id is in-process module state: it survives the reload teardown but is correctly dropped on process death (the next launch re-resolves) — no sidecar/mapping, consistent with epic I-1.\\\",\\n      \\\"Pre-existing lhc green-verify immutability drift on packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts (file byte-unchanged vs HEAD but mismatching the manifest hash from the Epic 05 closeout) is unrelated to this story; lhc verify (build/typecheck/lint/boundaries + 388 tests) passes.\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"openQuestions\\\": []\\n  },\\n  \\\"openQuestions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Is LHC's deterministic provider acceptable as the Story-1 interim production provider for observe-only Epic 1 (never invoked in Story 1; replaced by the PI-auth ModelCall in Story 5)? A real completing inference is blocked on @earendil-works/pi-ai not yet being a build dependency.\\\",\\n    \\\"Confirm against the real PI dependency: the launch-flag spelling for the named-session mode (--session vs --session-id) and whether a PI input surface exists for an interactive --resume picker (the default now resumes the most-recent cwd thread).\\\",\\n    \\\"Title policy: the follow-up directed adding title metadata, so connector-created threads use the cwd leaf as a provisional creation-time title; TDQ Q4's richer derivation (e.g. first user prompt, Story 2+) remains deferred — confirm the cwd-leaf default is acceptable until then.\\\",\\n    \\\"Pre-existing lhc immutability drift on packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts makes `pnpm --filter lhc green-verify` fail at the immutability step independent of this story; should it be re-baselined (out of this story's scope; not touched here)?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specDeviations\\\": [\\n    \\\"Production SDK provider for Story 1 is LHC's deterministic provider (interim), not the PI-auth-backed ModelCall (Story 5) — the completing-inference package (@earendil-works/pi-ai) is not yet a build dependency. Documented; the provider is never invoked in Story 1 because capture (Story 2) is not wired.\\\",\\n    \\\"--resume production selection defaults to the most-recent cwd-scoped thread (no interactive input surface in the local PI types yet); the picker module remains fully cwd-scoped/titled and selection-injectable.\\\",\\n    \\\"Reload reconstruction uses module-level in-process state for the durable resolved id (survives the reload teardown; dropped on process death) rather than a PI-session→thread mapping or a recovery sidecar (epic I-1).\\\",\\n    \\\"resolveThread/pickThread take injected deps (cwd, registryPath, new-thread file path/title, selection) rather than the tech-design sketch's `(launch, pi: ExtensionAPI)` / `(cwd)` — ExtensionAPI carries none of those.\\\",\\n    \\\"New thread title at creation = cwd leaf (`defaultThreadTitle`), a provisional Story-1 label; richer derivation is the deferred TDQ Q4.\\\",\\n    \\\"A-8 added `ambiguous_thread_id` to lhc ErrorCode and a registry v2 migration (cwd) with migrate-on-read (carried from the initial implementation).\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"recommendedNextStep\\\": \\\"Re-verify Story 1. Then proceed to Story 2 (Event Capture and Turn Derivation) on the lifecycle seam. When @earendil-works/pi-ai and the PI extension packages become build dependencies, replace the deterministic interim provider with the PI-auth ModelCall (Story 5) and wire an interactive --resume picker; optionally re-baseline the unrelated lhc retirement.test.ts manifest entry.\\\"\\n}\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":5212,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":462707,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":5212},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\",\"uuid\":\"96a3d34b-41f5-407f-9759-623988a39bb0\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cc2aLGidz5rkUX8pcjucT\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/005-continue.stdout.log:2350:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":1364571,\"duration_api_ms\":1345678,\"ttft_ms\":9416,\"ttft_stream_ms\":8979,\"time_to_request_ms\":60,\"num_turns\":36,\"result\":\"{\\n  \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"ready-for-verification\\\",\\n  \\\"planSummary\\\": \\\"Addressed all three blocking verifier findings (SV-001/002/003) while keeping Story 1 scope. SV-001 (production path was a placeholder): removed the fail-closed `inferenceNotConfigured` default and the null `--resume` selector; `activate()`/`createConnector()` now default to a real, construction-valid observe-only SDK config (LHC's exported `createDeterministicProvider`, background mode) and a real `--resume` selector (resume the most-recent cwd thread). session_start now actually resolves/creates the thread and initializes LHC on the production path. The deterministic provider is a documented interim: Epic 1 is observe-only and Story 1 does not capture yet (message_end is a no-op), so no derivation work is queued and the provider is never invoked — a real *completing* `ModelCall` cannot be written until `@earendil-works/pi-ai` becomes a build dependency (Story 5). SV-002 